  "claim": "Harry Ransom served as the Chancellor of this institute from 1961 to 1971. This institute and the place where Steven J. Kachelmeier got his Ph.D. combine to have both a 2000 acre campus and over 216,000 students.",
  "evidencia": "Page: University of Florida. Sentence: The University of Florida (commonly referred to as Florida or UF) is an American public land-grant, sea-grant, and space-grant research university on a 2000 acre campus in Gainesville, Florida.\nPage: University of Texas System. Sentence: The UT System is headquartered in Austin, and has a total enrollment of over 216,000 students (largest university system in Texas) and employs more than 87,000 faculty and staff.\nPage: Steven J. Kachelmeier. Sentence: Dr. Kachelmeier received his B.B.A. from the University of New Mexico and his Ph.D. from the University of Florida.\nPage: Harry Ransom. Sentence: Harry Huntt Ransom (November 22, 1908 – April 19, 1976) was a faculty member and administrator at the University of Texas, becoming the university's president in 1960, and ultimately served as the Chancellor of the University of Texas System from 1961 to 1971.",
