        "original_id": "75b33d57-4b9b-5064-ad2a-a08b061acd83",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Florida, University of Texas System\n- People: Steven J. Kachelmeier, Harry Huntt Ransom\n- Places: Gainesville, Florida, Austin, Texas\n- Roles: university president, Chancellor\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Huntt Ransom was born on November 22, 1908, and died on April 19, 1976.\n- The University of Florida is an American public land-grant, sea-grant, and space-grant research university on a 2,000-acre campus in Gainesville, Florida.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom was a faculty member and administrator at the University of Texas and became the university's president in 1960.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom served as Chancellor of the University of Texas System from 1961 to 1971.\n- The University of Texas System is headquartered in Austin and has over 216,000 students and more than 87,000 faculty and staff.\n- Steven J. Kachelmeier received his B.B.A. from the University of New Mexico and his Ph.D. from the University of Florida.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
